def fibonacci(n, memo={}):
    if n in memo:
        return memo[n]
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    memo[n] = fibonacci(n-1, memo) + fibonacci(n-2, memo)
    return memo[n]
``` 

This solution uses memoization to store the results of previously computed Fibonacci numbers in a dictionary called `memo`. This avoids redundant calculations and significantly improves the performance of the function for large values of `n`.
